  "narrative": {
    "intro": "KBR Wyle Services has $531M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, spread across 132 awards with an average award size of $4M. Obligations are down 17.0% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $278M in FY21 to a peak of $640M in FY25, then moved to $531M in FY26. National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the largest buyer, with $339M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Interior, Department of Defense, Department of Commerce, and Department of Transportation are the next largest buyers, with $71.5M, $53.8M, $40.2M, and $27.1M respectively. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) and Engineering Services are the top markets, with $147M and $131M respectively. Computer Facilities Management Services and related computing infrastructure services also appear among the top markets, with $67.9M and $40.2M respectively. The mix of work centers on R&D, engineering, and IT infrastructure support, with smaller amounts in rehabilitation services, telecommunications, repair and maintenance, and flight training.",
